      premises: ["existence-of-prime-factorization", "euclid-lemma"],
      proofName: "Euclid's lemma",
      formula: String.raw`n = p_1^{e_1} \cdots p_k^{e_k}`,
      text: "Every natural number n > 1 has a prime factorization, and it is unique up to the order of the factors.",
      proof: "Existence is the lemma. For uniqueness, a prime of one factorization divides the product of the other, so by Euclid's lemma it equals one of its factors; cancel it and use induction.",
